Decision: no static mathematical/control-flow blocker found; cleared for the bounded independent oracle gate, not runtime acceptance.

The logical prerequisite is one compatible partition under the declared model. Two checked alternatives suffice for ambiguity; one candidate requires exhaustive uniqueness or a sound shortcut. The finite positive-projection language criterion is both necessary and sufficient for unconstrained regular factors. Missing swap edges do not establish distinct ownership or observational ambiguity. Finite consistent no-K labels always admit the one-block partition. Contradictory labels are explicitly incompatible by this API, not syntax-invalid; malformed words/counts remain invalid.

Sparse unary counts correctly handle absent zero counts, empty P/N, duplicate raw observations and distinct positives supplying unary images. Known k1 is selected only after all labels are validated and contradictions excluded. Constructive two-coarsening code is entered only with1<k<r; split=r-k+1 lies between2 and r-1, giving two distinct k-block partitions. No-K constructive alternatives differ when r>1. Endpoints k1/kr and r1 are handled separately.

Swap certificates are exact opposing-label adjacent unequal transpositions and only successful unions are retained, forming a sound forest. All symbols, including unseen isolates, enter atoms. Trusted k>r is impossible by coarsening. Feasible atoms give exactly all their coarsenings; rejected atoms with k=r give zero because they are the only permitted candidate. Otherwise search proceeds even with no edges. The graph-failure-yet-unique example must exercise this actual fallback in the bounded gate.

The implementation uses incremental canonical RGS, rather than the subset-block recursion presented first in the theory. Assigning each ordered atom to an existing block or the next new block visits each unordered atom partition exactly once. Current-blockcount>k and current-blockcount+remaining<k pruning are sound, including at leaves. There is no unsafe partial-negative-coverage pruning or eager exponential table. A bounded4096-entry rejection-mask cache can evict/recompute without changing exact results. Leaf witnesses allocate new block lists and do not alias mutable DFS masks. Each negative gets one actual rejecting block reference. Stop-two is proof-complete for ambiguity; exhaustion-one/zero supports unique/incompatible. Interrupts before final emission conservatively return unresolved rather than leaking a provisional choice.

Deadline validation accepts finite integers and finite floats, rejecting booleans/nonfinite floats. Parsing/sorting/hashing/native allocation and JSON serialization remain cooperatively uninterruptible; hard capture ceilings are required. Resource/interrupt/recursion exceptions return unresolved. Unexpected CLI program/environment errors also return unresolved with stderr traceback; the independent audit must inspect raw execution evidence rather than treat them as successful observational-insufficiency decisions. Only certified_unique releases partition; no model/truth file is consumed.

Implementation supports a single explicit exact known_k, not the theory's general allowed-count sets. The audit uses singleton known-K slices only. The theory's optional monotonic rejection pruning is not implemented; no runtime claim for that pruning is made. Physical identifiability remains conditional on actual hardware satisfying the declared independence/disjoint/noise-free model and any trusted count. Static review does not certify those assumptions or runtime correctness.
